You are implementing **Phase 1** of the poker settlement contracts plan (`manamesh-games/manamesh/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-19-poker-hand-settler.md`). You do NOT need to read the plan file — full task specs are in this prompt.

## Working directory

All Solidity work goes in: `/Users/cyotee/Development/github-cyotee/manamesh-games/packages/poker/`

The Foundry workspace is already configured:
- `foundry.toml`: src=contracts, test=tests/foundry, solc 0.8.30, evm prague, optimizer_runs=1
- `remappings.txt`:
  - `forge-std/=lib/forge-std/src/`
  - `@openzeppelin/contracts/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/`
  - `@crane/contracts/=lib/crane/contracts/`
  - `@crane/test/=lib/crane/test/`
- Libraries already installed in `lib/`: forge-std v1.16.1, openzeppelin-contracts v5.0.2, cyotee/crane (latest main)
- `contracts/` and `tests/foundry/` directories exist but are empty.

A smoke-test compile of `@crane/contracts/interfaces/IFacet.sol` has been verified to work, so the toolchain is healthy.

## Architectural context

This is the off-chain-signed settlement layer for Texas Hold'em poker. Three EIP-712 typed structs are signed by players off-chain, then verified on-chain by a `PokerHandSettler` Diamond:
- `HandInit` — signed by every player to start a hand. handId is derived from it: `keccak256(abi.encode(HandInit fields))`. Players in `players[]` are sorted ascending by address; `buyIns[]` and `playerHandNonces[]` are parallel arrays.
- `HandOutcome` — signed at showdown. `winners[]` and `payouts[]` are parallel; `finalStacks[]` is parallel to `HandInit.players[]`; `holeCards[][]` is parallel to players (2 cards each, encoded as `(rank<<4)|suit` in a `uint8`); `communityCards[5]` are the revealed board.
- `RoundStateTransition` — signed at the end of each betting round, used by force-timeout settlement to prove the pot at the cutoff.

Subsequent phases (which you are NOT building now) will use these structs + libraries to implement the settler, oracle, and verifier facets.

## What to implement

### Task 1.1: Three struct files

Create exactly:

`contracts/types/HandInit.sol`:
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
pragma solidity 0.8.30;

/// @notice Off-chain unanimously-signed payload that fully describes a hand.
///         handId = keccak256(abi.encode(HandInit fields)).
/// @dev players[] MUST be sorted ascending. buyIns[] and playerHandNonces[]
///      MUST be parallel to players[].
struct HandInit {
    address[] players;
    uint256[] buyIns;
    address vault;
    uint256 smallBlind;
    uint256 bigBlind;
    uint256 timeoutSeconds;
    bytes32 otherConfig;
    uint256[] playerHandNonces;
}

bytes32 constant HAND_INIT_TYPEHASH = keccak256(
    "HandInit(address[] players,uint256[] buyIns,address vault,uint256 smallBlind,uint256 bigBlind,uint256 timeoutSeconds,bytes32 otherConfig,uint256[] playerHandNonces)"
);
```

`contracts/types/HandOutcome.sol`:
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
pragma solidity 0.8.30;

/// @notice Off-chain signed payload at showdown. holeCards[][] is parallel to
///         HandInit.players[]; each inner has 2 cards encoded as (rank<<4)|suit.
struct HandOutcome {
    bytes32 handId;
    uint256 pot;
    address[] winners;
    uint256[] payouts;
    uint256[] finalStacks;
    bytes32 finalStateHash;
    uint8[2][] holeCards;
    uint8[5] communityCards;
}

bytes32 constant HAND_OUTCOME_TYPEHASH = keccak256(
    "HandOutcome(bytes32 handId,uint256 pot,address[] winners,uint256[] payouts,uint256[] finalStacks,bytes32 finalStateHash,uint8[2][] holeCards,uint8[5] communityCards)"
);
```

`contracts/types/RoundStateTransition.sol`:
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
pragma solidity 0.8.30;

struct RoundStateTransition {
    bytes32 handId;
    uint8 roundNumber;
    uint256 currentPot;
    uint256[] playerStacks;
    bytes32 actionHash;
}

bytes32 constant ROUND_STATE_TRANSITION_TYPEHASH = keccak256(
    "RoundStateTransition(bytes32 handId,uint8 roundNumber,uint256 currentPot,uint256[] playerStacks,bytes32 actionHash)"
);
```

### Task 1.2: HandIdLib (TDD)

Create `contracts/lib/HandIdLib.sol`:
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
pragma solidity 0.8.30;

import {HandInit} from "../types/HandInit.sol";

library HandIdLib {
    // tag::handIdOf[]
    /// @custom:signature handIdOf((address[],uint256[],address,uint256,uint256,uint256,bytes32,uint256[]))
    function handIdOf(HandInit memory h) internal pure returns (bytes32) {
        return keccak256(abi.encode(
            h.players,
            h.buyIns,
            h.vault,
            h.smallBlind,
            h.bigBlind,
            h.timeoutSeconds,
            h.otherConfig,
            h.playerHandNonces
        ));
    }
    // end::handIdOf[]
}
```

Test: `tests/foundry/lib/HandIdLib.t.sol`. Test scenarios required:
- `test_handIdIsDeterministic` — same input → same output.
- `test_handIdChangesWhenPlayersChange`
- `test_handIdChangesWhenBuyInsChange`
- `test_handIdChangesWhenNonceChanges`

Use a `_makeHandInit()` helper that constructs a 2-player baseline; mutate one field per test. Import paths from `tests/foundry/lib/` going up: `../../../contracts/types/HandInit.sol` and `../../../contracts/lib/HandIdLib.sol`.

### Task 1.3: SignatureLib (TDD)

Create `contracts/lib/SignatureLib.sol`:
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
pragma solidity 0.8.30;

/// @notice EIP-712 signature helpers used by the poker settler.
/// @dev Domain separator is computed by the consuming contract; this library
///      only does digest building + recovery.
library SignatureLib {
    /// @custom:signature InvalidSignature(uint256,address)
    error InvalidSignature(uint256 index, address expected);
    /// @custom:signature LengthMismatch(uint256,uint256)
    error LengthMismatch(uint256 a, uint256 b);
    /// @custom:signature MalformedSignature(uint256)
    error MalformedSignature(uint256 length);

    function recoverEIP712(
        bytes32 domainSeparator,
        bytes32 structHash,
        bytes memory signature
    ) internal pure returns (address) {
        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
        return _recover(digest, signature);
    }

    function requireSignedByAll(
        bytes32 domainSeparator,
        bytes32 structHash,
        address[] memory signers,
        bytes[] memory sigs
    ) internal pure {
        if (signers.length != sigs.length) revert LengthMismatch(signers.length, sigs.length);
        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < signers.length; ++i) {
            address recovered = _recover(digest, sigs[i]);
            if (recovered != signers[i]) revert InvalidSignature(i, signers[i]);
        }
    }

    function _recover(bytes32 digest, bytes memory sig) private pure returns (address) {
        if (sig.length != 65) revert MalformedSignature(sig.length);
        bytes32 r;
        bytes32 s;
        uint8 v;
        assembly {
            r := mload(add(sig, 32))
            s := mload(add(sig, 64))
            v := byte(0, mload(add(sig, 96)))
        }
        return ecrecover(digest, v, r, s);
    }
}
```

Test: `tests/foundry/lib/SignatureLib.t.sol`. Required test scenarios:
